 "title": "A local rule grows the logical number line",
 "subject": "Whether a uniform rule acting only at open ends can grow a space whose bond distance is a ruler",
 "conclusion": "Starting from one parity knot, growing only at knots that hold two or more open ends grows exactly the two-way thread, a path of knots each keeping one open loop, whatever choices are made. Its bond distance counts the knots between two points plus one, so a rule that reads nothing but open ends grows a ruler of dimension one in both directions.",
